    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (78.68) and **Junior Caminero** (76.88), our two strongest plays. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Flaherty, with his elite 0.444 xwOBA driving a projection that survives park factor headwinds. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** is positioned to exploit a favorable 4.85 xERA from Me. Kelly; his projection is significantly bolstered by an impressive +19% SP skill adjustment and a prime spot in the heart of the order. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused strategy today, as **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.03) presents a vital start; his matchup against Woodruff offers a rare opportunity to exploit a slow delivery, pushing his projection nearly 30 points into \"Strong\" territory due to the high probability of stolen bases, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench was **Jacob Gonzalez**, whose 44.32 score landed him in \"Marginal\" territory, narrowly missing the cut behind the superior efficiency of **Chase Meidroth**. While **Jacob Gonzalez** offers baseline utility, he is currently buried in the #9 slot, which effectively neutered his production potential compared to the primary lineup. We also see high-leverage platoon edges for **Lars Nootbaar**, whose dynamic R/R platoon splits provide a +11% boost against Phillips, and **Kyle Schwarber**, who maintains a strong 67.89 score despite a slightly less favorable park. Managers should remain wary of **Christian Yelich** (55.76); while he remains a start, his score is currently dampened by a -13% platoon penalty against Rolison. We are monitoring all lineups closely, particularly for those marked \"Lineup Pending,\" to ensure that defensive switches or late-scratches do not force a pivot from our current optimal configuration.",
